%% CALL decision flow - LIVE code path only. Traced from Trading.Worker/SignalWorker.cs RunForSymbol -> DefaultInstrumentStrategy -> StrategyManager.SelectSignalAsync -> StrategySelectorService.Select -> StrategyManager.RunDirectional -> SignalEngineService.GenerateSignalDetailed -> EvaluateCall -> BuildSignalResult (SignalBuilder).
%% READING GUIDE: every diamond is phrased as the PASS test. YES = condition holds, flow continues. NO = rejection node (stadium shape) carrying the exact reason string / BlockedBy from code.
%% COMPILED DEFAULT =/= LIVE VALUE. StrategySettings rows live in the database (read through StrategySettingsService, 5 min cache). IMPORTANT RULE (StrategySettingsService.cs:171 IsSettingActive): for every condition guarded by Active(key) a MISSING row means NOT ACTIVE, so the condition is ABSENT. Then the compiled default threshold is never used for that key. Live thresholds = UNKNOWN from code, need SELECT on StrategySettings (SettingKey, Symbol, SettingValue, IsActive).
%% LIVE vs DEAD: CallEntryEvaluator.cs and PutEntryEvaluator.cs (Trading.SignalEngine/Services) are NOT referenced by any live code, not by DI, not by tests, not by Trading.Backtest. They are stale copies (use 1m RSI, EnableCandleFilter on CALL, no pullback band, no gap-up PCR exemption). Also never referenced anywhere: CandleConfirmation.cs (used only by those two dead classes), OptionLegSelector.cs, SignalResultFactory.cs, SignalConfidenceCalculator.cs. The LIVE CALL spec is SignalEngineService.EvaluateCall. Trading.Backtest EntryEvaluator calls the same SignalEngineService.EvaluateCall via InternalsVisibleTo (EntryEvaluator.cs:774).
%% NOT PRESENT (no such condition in live CALL code): CALL entry condition on 1m RSI (1m RSI only feeds confidence score and MarketClassification), LTP above VWAP inside the AND chain (condition 3 not wired, Vwap argument is passed but never read by EvaluateCall, VWAP only enters via flag-gated VwapSideGate), Volume above VolumeSMA20 (condition 8 not wired, no volume read by EvaluateCall), 5m EMA trend alignment inside the AND chain (EnableCall5mTrendFilter is not read by live code, TrendBullish input is computed but unused), previous-candle LOW for CALL, hardcoded per-symbol exceptions in the CALL AND chain (only the BANKNIFTY PUT breakdown rule is symbol-hardcoded and it is PUT), time-of-day window inside the engine (NoTradeWindowGate is commented out in SignalWorker.cs:63), gap-up/gap-down session exemptions except the CALL PCR minimum exemption and the opening RSI band override, PriceChangePct vs open as an always-on CALL condition (only via PriceChangeThreshold row).
%% SYMBOL EXCEPTIONS actually present: per-symbol StrategySettings rows (exact Symbol row wins over global row, an inactive symbol row switches the feature off for that symbol), per-symbol dictionaries in TradingSettings (liquidity, ATR thresholds in MarketRegimeService for NIFTY/BANKNIFTY/FINNIFTY/SENSEX/MIDCAPNIFTY), no other.
